  <h2 id="open-gates">Blocking Gates Before Mainnet</h2>
  <p>
    <code>v1 (v3.0.0-rfc)</code> is a pre-implementation RFC and does <strong>not</strong> authorize mainnet deployment.
    <strong>Stage 0</strong> (zero bridge custody) blocks on: a tagged <code>go-zenon</code> release containing
    <code>0aa299e</code> + <code>DynamicPlasmaSpork</code> enforced, upstream issue <code>#239</code> closure + FIFO
    panic-recovery fuzz gate (<strong>B1</strong>), full <code>SetPlasmaVariables</code> pinning including
    <code>MaxBasePlasmaInMomentum &ge; 2,100,000</code>, <code>MaxPriceChangePercent &le; 25</code>, targets, and
    denominator (<strong>B2</strong>), 1-/2-block SHA-256 coinbase midstate conformance vectors, and Signet&harr;Zenon
    PTLC/LN adversarial tests (<code>72</code>-blk CSV, <code>2.3&times;</code> slow-block margin).
    <strong>Stage 1A (<code>BitVMX</code> Sovereign ZK Rollup)</strong> additionally blocks on: empirical Signet
    measurement of all <code>n = 8</code> <code>BitVMX-CPU</code> TRUC v3 dispute txs &amp; 256-bit Lamport
    <code>TakeTx</code> scripts, immutable <code>vk_STF</code> prover/verifier benchmarks, independent external
    cryptography &amp; Bitcoin Script audits, and verified commitment of <code>~12.8–18.8 BTC</code> of independent
    operator/verifier BTC capital (or selection of the <strong>Stage 1B <code>clArk</code></strong> alternative gate).
  </p>
</SpecShell>
